course: dictionary
lesson: 8939
title: Many meanings of silence
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and context tells you which one you need. «Silence, please» means stop talking. «A minute's silence» means a short time of quiet to remember someone. Read the words around the word before you decide.
explain: «Bullies often say "Don't tell or it will be worse", because they rely on silence.» Here silence does not mean quiet music or a quiet room. It means nobody speaks up about the bullying. Bullies want silence so the problem stays hidden, which is why telling a trusted adult makes bullying stop.
explain: In music, «a rest is a counted silence and is part of the bar.» The silence still has a beat and a place in the tune. It is part of the music, not a gap where nothing happens.
fact: Silence means there is no sound at all, or people are not talking.
fact: To silence means to make someone or something quiet.
fact: «A minute's silence» is a short time when people stay quiet to remember someone.
fact: «Silence lets hate spread», so hateful comments should always be reported.
fact: Useful phrases: in silence, break the silence, an awkward silence.
exercise: The teacher says, «Silence, please.» What does silence mean here? | Running to the door | Asking a question | *Making no sound and not talking | Singing loudly together
exercise: Everyone stood for «a minute's silence» on Remembrance Day. Why did they do this? | To start a race | *To remember someone | To make a cake | To practise a song
exercise: The teacher used a whistle to silence the noisy class. What does silence mean here? | To give them lunch | To paint the walls | *To make them quiet | To shout loudly
test: Bullies often say «Don't tell», because they rely on silence. What does the silence help the bully do? | Win a prize | *Keep the bullying hidden | Make friends with everyone | Stop being unkind
test: In music, «a rest is a counted silence». What is a rest? | A tune played on the piano | A mistake in the music | *A timed gap with no sound that is part of the bar | A loud note played twice
exam: Which is the best reason to tell a trusted adult about bullying? | So that the bully can become your friend | Bullies like it when you keep quiet | Silence always makes things better | *Telling them is the way bullying stops
